def snap(rawA, E, inside, r, sc, hidden):
    """1 November 2026 : the template gives one seed per part, the image gives the boundaries : each connected piece of a part is eroded to a seed (a thin piece keeps its core), then a watershed on the edge map : a boundary lands on a line when there is one, and midway between the seeds, which is the template's own place, when there is none. Specks of the template (stray polygons, parts poking through) make no seed."""
